> New rule:  never leave a wand lying around.  Even a cursed one.

Good rule.  If possible don't leave potions around either (!sleep
sucks) but that's much lower priority than never leaving unattended
wands unless you know they're safe (light, enlightenment, sdd, etc).

Cursed wands aren't a major problem in general (something like 1%
chance of blowing up and 99% chance of functioning normally).  If it's
vital (wishing, death, teleportation) it's worth uncursing, if it's
just surplus use until it blows and be happy.

> I thought that bonepile curses don't extend to stuff inside containers.

They don't, but you don't want to loot bags until you uncurse them or
you could lose a lot of what's inside.  Unless you have an emergency
need for some items, the original poster's plan to leave the bags
untouched until he/she can /cancel them or otherwise safely loot is
ideal.

Unless, of course, you know they're regular or oilskin sacks.



